{"id": "80a228ee-a5e0-417e-8052-35efc1af2faf", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T07:11:48.849977", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "336026ce-5aad-4b22-a2e7-a9d8ccbda5f3", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-a0dcc547-bc5b-4b3b-b9ef-df1cd9fe70da", "tool_call": {"id": "call-a0dcc547-bc5b-4b3b-b9ef-df1cd9fe70da", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose plan skeleton for ACF-based cycle length selection\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"Inspection report and approach skeleton as requested. Workspace contains only /workspace/task.json (design-only per inline track.md: \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"). No CycleNet / period-selection / ACF code is present. Context summary covers CycleNet (RPL module, learnable periodic embedding indexed by t mod L, with cycle length L as the key hyperparameter) and ACF-based period detection (peaks at integer multiples of the true period, Bartlett 95% band ±1.96/√n). Proposed skeleton: (a) synthetic ground-truth series + ETT/Weather/Traffic/Electricity benchmarks; (b) combined candidate set L_cand = grid G ∪ ACF-informed A, |L_cand|≤~25; (c) ACF on training fold only, stationary if needed, mean/variance-weighted pooling across channels; (d) four ACF selectors — argmax, first-significant-peak, cumulative-harmonic score, prominence-based — with ε=0.02 tie-break preferring smaller L; (e) fixed CycleNet hyperparameters except L, rolling-window validation, MSE/MAE at horizons {96,192,336,720} × 3 seeds; (f) controls C0 Oracle, C1 Default (L=24), C2 Random, C3–C6 the four ACF variants, C7 grid-search upper bound; headline metric = gap-to-oracle MSE. Six open items flagged for researcher decision: (i) identification-accuracy vs forecasting-performance as the headline goal (recommend both), (ii) per-channel vs pooled ACF semantics (recommend pooled to match single-L CycleNet), (iii) handling of non-stationary / multi-seasonal series (smallest peak vs LCM of peaks), (iv) Bartlett band + Bonferroni/block-bootstrap for pooling plus tie-break rule, (v) explicit computational budget table (no GPU, no preinstalled deps, network disabled), (vi) confirmation of CycleNet period-parameter semantics since no code/doc is present in the repo. Awaiting researcher approval / clarifications before producing the full design.\",\"evidence\":\"Workspace inspection: `ls -la /workspace` and `find /workspace -type f` show a single file, /workspace/task.json. `cat /workspace/task.json` reveals documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" Public task envelope confirms empty repositories and datasets lists, gpu_enabled=false, network=disabled. No README, no CycleNet code, no ACF/period-selection code anywhere on disk. Repository is consistent with a design-only deliverable; any CycleNet-specific parameter semantics must be sourced from the published paper (Lin et al., NeurIPS 2023) rather than local code.\",\"assumptions\":\"[-] ACF is computed on the training fold only to avoid test leakage. [-] CycleNet uses a single shared cycle length L across all channels of the periodic embedding (per the original paper). [-] 95% Bartlett band ±1.96/√n is the reference for \\\"significant\\\" ACF peaks. [-] Standard long-horizon forecast horizons {96, 192, 336, 720} are appropriate for the chosen benchmarks. [-] MSE/MAE are reported per horizon and per dataset, averaged over 3 seeds. [-] |L_cand| will be bounded ≤ ~25 to keep the sweep tractable under the budget (no GPU, no preinstalled deep-learning deps, network disabled).\",\"uncertainties\":\"[-] Goal priority: identification accuracy vs forecasting performance (recommend both, forecasting as headline). [-] Per-channel vs pooled ACF semantics relative to CycleNet's single L. [-] Treatment of multi-seasonal / non-stationary series (smallest peak, LCM of peaks, or hierarchical). [-] Statistical correction for pooled ACF across channels (Bonferroni vs block-bootstrap) and final tie-break rule. [-] Feasible computational budget given no GPU and no preinstalled dependencies; exact datasets and horizons must be locked before the full design. [-] Exact semantics of CycleNet's period parameter across forks / re-implementations, since no local code documents it.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-e18152bb-684b-4d10-8748-6fa4cb16375a", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 10}
